@startuml
title Interaction of Model with View and AppWrapper

actor "User (View)" as User
participant "Model (modeld)" as Model
participant "AppWrapper (app_wrapperd)" as AppWrapper
participant "Console Utility" as Util

== Initialization ==
Model -> Model : Loads JSON plugins\n(creates main menu and task screens)
Model -> User : Sends first StateChanged signal

== Navigation ==
User -> Model : SelectScreen(screenId)
Model -> Model : Updates currentScreenId,\nnavigation stack
Model -> User : StateChanged (new screen)

== Changing parameters ==
User -> Model : SetParameter(taskId, paramId, value)
Model -> Model : Updates appParams
Model -> User : StateChanged (updated controls)

== Running a task ==
User -> Model : Execute(taskId)
Model -> Model : Builds arguments,\nsubstitutes params
Model -> AppWrapper : Start(appId, args, env, options)
AppWrapper -> AppWrapper : Starts the process
AppWrapper -> Model : Started(pid)
Model -> Model : Sets status to "running",\nupdates controls
Model -> User : StateChanged (screen with "Stop" button)

== Output processing ==
loop For each line of stdout/stderr
    AppWrapper -> Model : Output(stream, data)
    Model -> Model : Applies parsing rules\n(updates controls)
    Model -> User : StateChanged (updated data)
end

== Completion / error ==
AppWrapper -> Model : Exited(code, signal) or Error(message)
Model -> Model : Updates status,\nfinal controls
Model -> User : StateChanged (final state)

== Interactive input (optional) ==
User -> Model : SendInput(taskId, data)
Model -> AppWrapper : SendInput(path, data)
AppWrapper -> Util : Writes to STDIN (or PTY)

@enduml
